---
import Base from '../components/Base.astro';
import '@/styles/index.scss'
import Expandable from '@/components/Expandable';
---

<Base class="home-page">
	<Expandable startExpanded title="Mission Statement">
		Often the best solutions can be found by slowing down. In this high-speed world, pacing ourselves is a powerful act of resistance. My game engine is closer to your beloved beater car that will never die than to the high-maintenance sports car. Taking it apart is half of the experience.
	</Expandable>
	<Expandable startExpanded title="Technical Explanation" client:load>
		<p class="intro">This game engine is a synthesis of my many years of experience in many areas of coding including emphasis on web development and game development. Being highly modular makes it easy to mix and match libraries and to add support for new ones. State management is handled using my own <a href="https://github.com/L1lith/Jabr">universal state management library Jabr</a>, which is very simple and has no ecosystem lock-in. It's unlike most state libraries which tend to be locked in to rendering libraries like React or SolidJS, making it perfect for fusing the domains of web development and game development.<br/><br/>This game engine strongly leverages the benefits of being written in a Functional Programming (FP) style instead of Objected Oriented Programming (OOP) while still having some resemblance to OOP by using a style that is a variation of <a href="https://www.daydreamsoft.com/blog/ecs-vs-oop-in-large-scale-games-choosing-the-right-architecture-for-performance-and-scalability">Entity Component System (ECS) style game development</a>. In line with Functional Programming ethos every part of my game engine was built to maximize separations of concerns & interchangeability.</p>
	</Expandable>
</Base>
